		<div class="plate-grid">
			<div class="legend">
				<h1 id="plate-1">A research assistant that shows its evidence.</h1>
				<p class="lead">Sub-Sub reads the papers in your Zotero library, finds the ones you are missing in PubMed, Europe PMC and OpenAlex, and writes notes that say what it read. You see every change to your library before it happens. It runs on your computer, in English or Portuguese.</p>

				<div class="install" data-tabs>
					<div class="install-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Install">
						<button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-unix" data-os="unix" aria-controls="panel-unix" aria-selected="true">macOS and Linux</button>
						<button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-win" data-os="windows" aria-controls="panel-win" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Windows</button>
						<button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-npm" aria-controls="panel-npm" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">npm</button>
					</div>
					<div class="install-panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-unix" aria-labelledby="tab-unix">
						<pre class="cmd"><code>curl -fsSL https://subsub.tiagojacinto.eu/<wbr>install.sh | sh</code></pre>
						<p>Paste in Terminal. It installs in your user folder; no administrator rights. <a href="/install/#about-the-install-command">What this command does</a>.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="install-panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-win" aria-labelledby="tab-win" hidden>
						<pre class="cmd ps"><code>powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c "irm https://subsub.tiagojacinto.eu/<wbr>install.ps1 | iex"</code></pre>
						<p>Paste in PowerShell. It installs in your user folder and adds a shortcut. <a href="/install/#about-the-install-command">What this command does</a>.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="install-panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-npm" aria-labelledby="tab-npm" hidden>
						<pre class="cmd"><code>npm install -g @tiagojct/subsub && subsub init</code></pre>
						<p>Needs Node.js 22.19 or later and uv. In pi: <code>pi install npm:@tiagojct/subsub</code>.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="hero-alt">You need Zotero and an account with a model provider; <a href="/models/#use-sub-sub-for-free">a free one is enough to try</a>. <a href="/install/">Install guide</a> · <a href="/guide/">The first half hour</a></p>
				<p class="newcomer">New to Zotero or to AI tools? <a href="/students/">Start here</a> · <a href="/pt/estudantes/" lang="pt-PT" hreflang="pt-PT">Para estudantes, em português</a><br>Clinical researcher? <a href="/clinicians/">What it does for you, and what it is not</a></p>
