<section class="plate" aria-labelledby="plate-2">
	<div class="wrap plate-mark">
		<p class="runhead"><span>Sub-Sub</span><span class="mid">What you get</span><span>Plate II.</span></p>
		<div class="split">
			<div>
				<h2 id="plate-2">Notes you can check, in plain text files.</h2>
				<p class="section-lead">Each note is a Markdown file in your Sub-Sub folder. Obsidian shows it well; any editor opens it.</p>
				<ul class="result-points">
					<li><strong>It says what it read.</strong> The full text, the abstract or only the metadata. Page numbers come only from a full text.</li>
					<li><strong>It cites only works it found.</strong> Library items by citekey; other works with their DOI or PMID.</li>
					<li><strong>You decide how much it writes.</strong> With <code>/read</code>, a note is quotes and questions, and you write the answers. Sub-Sub drafts text for a manuscript only when you ask.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<figure class="lines-fig">
				<div class="evidence-lines">
					<div class="ev ev-full"><span class="ev-no">6.</span><p class="ev-file">Literature/smith2021.md</p><p class="ev-field">evidence: <span>full text</span></p><p class="ev-desc">Quotes with their page, each linked to that page of the PDF.</p></div>
					<div class="ev ev-abstract"><span class="ev-no">7.</span><p class="ev-file">Literature/lind2020.md</p><p class="ev-field">evidence: <span>abstract</span></p><p class="ev-desc">Quotes from the abstract only, and no page numbers.</p></div>
					<div class="ev ev-meta"><span class="ev-no">8.</span><p class="ev-file">Literature/okafor2023.md</p><p class="ev-field">evidence: <span>metadata</span></p><p class="ev-desc">Only the title and the details of the record. The note says so.</p></div>
				</div>
				<figcaption><span class="sc">Figs. 6–8.</span> <i>The three evidence lines. The notes pane draws them the same way: a solid line for the full text, a dashed line for the abstract, a dotted line for the metadata.</i></figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="plate" aria-labelledby="plate-3">
	<div class="wrap plate-mark">
		<p class="runhead"><span>Sub-Sub</span><span class="mid">How a change happens</span><span>Plate III.</span></p>
		<h2 id="plate-3">You see the change before it happens. You can undo it after.</h2>
		<ol class="stages">
			<li class="stage ask"><span class="mark-line"></span><h3>You ask</h3><p>In plain language. For example: tag the next 10 items without a topic.</p></li>
			<li class="stage dry"><span class="mark-line"></span><h3>A dry run</h3><p>The preview shows each item, with each tag it adds and each tag it removes.</p></li>
			<li class="stage decide"><span class="mark-line"></span><h3>Yes or No</h3><p>The check is in the program, not in the instructions to the model. The model cannot skip it.</p></li>
			<li class="stage record"><span class="mark-line"></span><h3>The journal</h3><p>The change goes into a journal. <code>/undo</code> reverts it. Nothing is deleted: items go to the Zotero trash.</p></li>
		</ol>
	</div>
</section>

